      "node_id": "kg_doc_1",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "A Story of Floating Weeds (浮草物語 , Ukikusa monogatari ) is a 1934 silent film directed by Yasujirō Ozu which he later remade as \"Floating Weeds\" in 1959 in color. It won the Kinema Junpo Award for best film, the third consecutive year an Ozu film won, following \"I Was Born, But...\" and \"Passing Fancy\".",
